<% season = CurrentSeason.year %>
<% last_season = season.to_i - 1 %>
<% content_for :title, "Commissioner's Corner" %>
<% content_for :page_heading, "Commissioner's Corner #{season}" %>

<%# Unlike most pages this one runs the full width, with no sidebar logo, and its text isn't the site's purple. %>
<div class="ptfgPlainText">
  <p style="margin-bottom: 10px; font-size: larger">
    Welcome back, PTFG <b>Private League Commissioners</b>!
  </p>
  <span class="ccAlert-eyebrow">Please read</span>
  <div class="alert alert-danger ccAlert" role="alert">
    <div class="ccAlert-head">
      <p class="ccAlert-lead">
        Please take a few minutes to read everything on the page below. There are several important updates for the
        <%= season %> season including:
      </p>
    </div>
    <ol class="ccAlert-list">
      <li>
        <span class="ccAlert-text">
          There are no <b>Hawaii</b> tournaments this year so the <%= season %> PGA Tour season starts on January 21st
          this year.
        </span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="ccAlert-text">
          For the <b>TOUR Championship</b> season finale, PTFG has always used standard pro-rated earnings rather than the
          inflated FedEx Cup finale purse (e.g., $40 million). The PGA Tour’s major overhaul to a two-week, match-play
          format won't take effect until <b>2028</b>, so the 2027 season will remain unaffected. When the new format (and
          location) are fully announced, I plan to make adjustments similar to those I previously used to accommodate the
          Dell Match Play tournament.
        </span>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="card ptfgPanel">
    <div class="card-header ptfgBluePanelBackground">
      <h3 class="card-title"><b><%= season %> League Setup – Schedule, Settings & Payment</b></h3>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body ccSetup">
      <p class="ccSetup-lead">
        I can only begin setting up your league for the <%= season %> season once you provide your desired tournament
        schedule, number of segments, and any other changes. You can view the <%= season %> schedule
        <%= link_to 'here', "https://www.pgatour.com/schedule/#{season}", target: 'schedule' %>.
      </p>
      <div class="ccNote">
        <i class="bi bi-info-circle ccNote-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <div>
          Keep in mind that PTFG features only <b>one PGA TOUR tournament per week</b>, always selecting the
          <b>most prestigious event</b> when multiple tournaments are scheduled. The 4
          <i>opposite-field/alternate events</i> on the <%= season %> schedule will not be available, as supporting
          them would require significant website changes and could create unnecessary confusion for participants.
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="ccSection">
        <h4 class="ccSection-title"><i class="bi bi-calendar-event" aria-hidden="true"></i>Tournament Schedule</h4>
        <p>When submitting your schedule, please double-check that it reflects exactly what you want for <%= season %>:</p>
        <div class="ccOptions">
          <div class="ccOption ccOption--blue">
            <div class="ccOption-title"><i class="bi bi-arrow-repeat" aria-hidden="true"></i>Keeping the same format?</div>
            <p>
              Simply reply <b>Same as last year</b>. This means retaining the same number of tournaments and segments,
              along with the same starting and ending tournaments as <%= last_season %>, with the exception of the
              <i>Sony Open</i>, which is not being played in <%= season %>.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="ccOption ccOption--red">
            <div class="ccOption-title"><i class="bi bi-pencil-square" aria-hidden="true"></i>Want to make changes?</div>
            <p>
              Include the specific tournaments, segment structure, or other adjustments you'd like for <%= season %>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="ccHint">
          For reference, you can review last season's schedule by selecting <b><%= last_season %></b> on your league's
          <b>Schedule</b> page.  Interested in learning more about the changes to next year's PGA TOUR schedule?
          Check out the PGA TOUR's
          <%= link_to "#{season} schedule announcement", 'https://www.pgatour.com/article/news/latest/2026/08/26/pga-tour-announces-2027-schedule-through-tour-championship/',
                      :target => '_pgaAnnouncement' %>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ccSection">
        <h4 class="ccSection-title"><i class="bi bi-sliders" aria-hidden="true"></i>League Settings</h4>
        <p>
          Please also review your current <b>League Settings</b>, located under the <b>Home</b> tab on your league
          website. If you'd like to make any changes, let me know <b>before I set up your <%= season %> season</b>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ccSection">
        <h4 class="ccSection-title"><i class="bi bi-credit-card" aria-hidden="true"></i>League Fees &amp; Payment</h4>
        <p>
          As in previous years, payment is due <b>one month after your league season begins</b>. By that time, you
          should have your final team count. League pricing remains unchanged for <%= season %>:
        </p>
        <div class="ccPrices">
          <div class="ccPrice">
            <span class="ccPrice-amount"><%= MIN_LEAGUE_FEE %></span>
            <span class="ccPrice-label"><b>Minimum league fee</b>, covering up to 30 teams</span>
          </div>
          <div class="ccPrice">
            <span class="ccPrice-amount">$6</span>
            <span class="ccPrice-label"><b>Per additional team</b>, beyond the first 30, up to 100 teams</span>
          </div>
          <div class="ccPrice">
            <span class="ccPrice-amount">$1</span>
            <span class="ccPrice-label"><b>Per team after 100</b>, up to a maximum of 300 teams</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>You can review your league's payment information and calculate the total cost under:</p>
        <div class="ccPath">
          <b>Commish</b><i class="bi bi-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i><b>PTFG Payment</b>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card ptfgPanel">
    <div class="card-header ptfgGreenPanelBackground">
      <h3 class="card-title"><b>What's New For <%= season %> – Behind the Scenes</b></h3>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <p class="ccSetup-lead">
        I've spent much of this year upgrading the technology that powers PTFG. None of it changes how the game is
        played. Think of it as renovating a house while the family still lives in it: new wiring, new plumbing and a
        sturdier foundation, so everything keeps running well for years to come. Here's what has changed at a high
        level:
      </p>
      <ul class="ccItems ccItems--green">
        <li class="ccItem">
          <h4 class="ccItem-title"><i class="bi bi-hdd-network" aria-hidden="true"></i>A new, faster server</h4>
          <p>
            The computer server that stores PTFG data and deliver it to your web browser has been replaced
            with newer, faster, and more reliable one. Your league website address stays the same.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="ccItem">
          <h4 class="ccItem-title"><i class="bi bi-gear" aria-hidden="true"></i>Updated software</h4>
          <p>
            The software that runs your league website (lineups, results, standings and everything else) was built on
            technology that is well over a decade old and is no longer supported by its creators. It has been
            carried over to modern technology, which makes it easier to keep secure and easier to improve in the
            future. The rules, scoring, and features you know are the same.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="ccPatience">
        <span class="ccPatience-icon"><i class="bi bi-heart-fill" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
        <div>
          <h4 class="ccPatience-title">A few bumps and hiccups may happen along the way</h4>
          <p>
            Changes this big are never completely smooth. You might see a page that looks a little different, an email
            that arrives late, or something that doesn't work quite the way it used to. I've tested carefully, but if
            you run into anything, please <%= link_to "let me know", contact_us_path %> and I'll get it fixed as
            quickly as I can.
          </p>
          <p class="ccPatience-thanks">
            I truly appreciate everyone's patience and understanding as we make the move.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card ptfgPanel">
    <div class="card-header ptfgRedPanelBackground">
      <h3 class="card-title"><b>Reminders &amp; Other Tips</b></h3>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <ul class="ccItems ccItems--red">
        <li class="ccItem">
          <h4 class="ccItem-title"><i class="bi bi-arrow-clockwise" aria-hidden="true"></i>Pre-Loading With Last Year's Teams</h4>
          <p>
            Don’t forget, you can <b>pre-load your league with last year's teams</b>. It's the quickest way to get your
            league set up for the new season.
          </p>
          <ul class="ccBullets">
            <li>
              When you click the <b>Pre-Load Teams</b> button, each returning participant gets a <b>Welcome Back</b>
              email saying a new <%= season %> team has been created for them, with the same team name as last season.
            </li>
            <li>
              If someone from last year shouldn't get a new team, mark them as <b>Unsubscribed</b> under the User
              Settings tab <b>before</b> you run the pre-load.
            </li>
            <li>
              Members keep the same email address as last year for their Login ID. If they register with a different
              one, they may accidentally create a new user account, and then won't see their <%= season %> team when
              they log in with their old email.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <div class="ccNote ccNote--red">
            <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle ccNote-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <div>
              <b>IMPORTANT:</b><br>
              You should use the Pre-Load Teams feature before creating any new teams, as it becomes <b>unavailable</b>
              once the first <%= season %> team has been created. You can access this option from:
              <div class="ccPath ccPath--onRed">
                <b>Commish</b> (tab)<i class="bi bi-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i><b>Pre-Load Teams</b>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ccItem">
          <h4 class="ccItem-title"><i class="bi bi-trophy" aria-hidden="true"></i>Commissioner's Cup</h4>
          <p>
            The <b>Commissioner's Cup</b> has been one of our most popular optional contests since it was introduced a
            few years ago. It's a side competition with its own standings, played over tournaments <b>you choose</b>.
          </p>
          <ul class="ccBullets">
            <li>
              <b>You pick the tournaments</b> (at least four). They don't have to be majors, so it's like the Majors
              Contest, but with your own list.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Up to five prizes</b> can be awarded, and as with other contests, virtual trophies go to both the
              first- and last-place finishers.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Some ideas: if your league starts in early January, you could choose the eight signature events with the
            biggest purses. Or, to make the smaller events more meaningful, choose the tournaments with the lowest
            purses instead. It's entirely up to you, hence the name.
          </p>
          <p>
            <b>Want it for your league?</b> Contact me and send the list of tournaments you'd like to include, and I'll
            turn it on.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="ccItem">
          <h4 class="ccItem-title"><i class="bi bi-cash-coin" aria-hidden="true"></i>Save Yourself Some Agony</h4>
          <p>
            Don’t be one of those commissioners still chasing down league payments after the season ends. Two tools
            help:
          </p>
          <ul class="ccBullets">
            <li>
              <b>Email filter:</b> throughout the season, use the website's email filter to message only the members who
              haven't yet paid their league fee.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Lineup lockout:</b> an effective last resort for stragglers. It prevents unpaid members from submitting
              their weekly lineups until their fees are paid.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>You can find the lineup lockout under:</p>
          <div class="ccPath">
            <b>Commish</b> (tab)<i class="bi bi-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i><b>Users</b><i class="bi bi-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i><b>With <%= season %> Team</b><i class="bi bi-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i><b>Edit</b><i class="bi bi-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i><b>Lineup Lockout</b> (checkbox)
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ccItem">
          <h4 class="ccItem-title"><i class="bi bi-people" aria-hidden="true"></i>Looking for more participants?</h4>
          <p>
            I often hear from players who are interested in joining additional leagues. If your league is looking to add
            teams, I'd be happy to post a notice in those leagues and direct interested players to contact you through
            your league's website. I won't share your email address.
          </p>
          <p>A couple of requirements:</p>
          <ul class="ccBullets">
            <li>You must be <b>posting your league prizes via the website</b> each season.</li>
            <li>You must <b>pay them out in a timely manner</b>.</li>
          </ul>
          <p><b>Interested?</b> Just let me know.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
